      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Special Program Aid (Inventory Clerk) Agency Texas A&M International University Department College Of Nursing & Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary $17.00 hourly Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Job Summary   The Special Program Aid, under supervision, will be responsible for the inventory in the Health Science Division building and laboratory equipment physical inventory ensuring that inventory is properly received, recorded, tagged, delivered, closely monitored, and disposed of in accordance with retention policies and procedures. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist in management, review, and hosting inventory transaction database system through receiving, affixing, and recording inventory tags. Assists in development and conducting of daily cycle counting procedures to ensure inventory accuracy. Coordinates annual physical inventories. Analyzes obsolete inventory, calculates inventory risks, and communicates trends. Reports stolen or missing equipment in accordance with policies and procedures. Conducts periodic internal inventory audits. Coordinates equipment procurement and inventory control. Reconciles discrepancies in inventory and receives quantities from stores and vendors. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. Minimum Requirements Education – High school diploma or equivalent   Experience – One year of related experience. May not be a currently enrolled undergraduate student at Texas A&M International University. Knowledge and Abilities Knowledge of: Word processing, spreadsheet, and database applications. Ability to: Multitask and work cooperatively with others. Verbal and written communication skills.  Physical Requirements – General office environment The physical demands 