    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Instructional-Assistant-Professor-of-Special-Education_R-090324-1": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor of Special Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructional Assistant Professor of Special Education Agency Texas A&M International University Department Educational Programs Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Instructional Assistant Professor of Special Education to begin  Fall 2026 .  TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu . This is a non tenure-track Instructional Assistant Professor (9-month faculty position; 3-year appointment with the possibility of renewal based on annual evaluations and performance). Primary duties will include teaching 15 semester credit hours (the equivalent of five courses) per semester in various modalities including face-to-face and online undergraduate courses and online graduate courses. Duties also include mentoring students and providing service on departmental, college, university, and professional committees. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  The mission of the College of Education is to prepare highly effective, culturally competent educational professionals who are equipped to understand and assume leadership positions in a global society. Required Qualifications The successful candidate must hold a doctorate in Special Education or a related field. ABDs will also be considered but must have earned a doctorate before appointment. All specializations will be considered. We strongly encourage candidates with a strong record of working in the Special Education field in the public school setting, the ability to teach in areas that complement/strengthen our programs, hold State of Texas Special Education Teacher Certification and/or Educational Diagnostician Certification, preferred.  We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university. Application Process   The first review of applications will be  3/2/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/ . INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Adjunct-Instructor---Doctor-of-Physical-Therapy-Program--Hybrid-_R-095819-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Doctor of Physical Therapy Program (Hybrid)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty – Doctor of Physical Therapy Program (Hybrid) Agency Texas A&M International University Department College Of Nursing & Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Texas A&M International University (TAMIU) Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program has openings for part-time Adjunct Instructors appointed on a per-semester basis. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in the Doctor of Physical Therapy Program adds applicants to a pool that is available to the program for selection as instructional needs arise for Fall 2028 through Spring 2030. Minimum Educational Requirements Applicants must possess: An earned Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree or other academic doctoral degree in a related field from a regionally accredited institution. A current, active, and unencumbered physical therapist license in any United States jurisdiction (required for licensed physical therapist positions). Demonstrated content expertise appropriate for the assigned teaching responsibilities. Contemporary clinical experience and evidence of ongoing professional development are preferred. Board certification through the American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties (ABPTS) or other specialty certifications (e.g., OCS, SCS, NCS, PCS, CCS, GCS, WCS) are preferred when appropriate to the assigned content area. Duties and Responsibilities Adjunct instructors may be assigned to facilitate immersive laboratory experiences, assist with laboratory instruction, or teach didactic courses in one or more of the following areas within the Doctor of Physical Therapy curriculum: Structural Human Anatomy, Systems Screening and Basic Examination Skills, Therapeutic Exercise and Manual Therapy Techniques, Biomechanics and Kinesiology, Neuroscience for Physical Therapy, Diagnostic Imaging, Emergency Care Procedures, Business and Management in Physical Therapy, Diagnosis and Management of Musculoskeletal Conditions, Diagnosis and Management of Neurological Conditions, Diagnosis and Management of Cardiovascular, Pulmonary, Integumentary, Metabolic, and Endocrine Conditions. Must coordinate course administrative duties such as, but not limited to, grading student work, loading all course content, such as assessments and lecture modules, meeting with students, submitting grades in a timely manner, meeting census and grade deadlines, and additional administrative duties as needed. Application Procedure: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Completed employment applications must include: Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest addressing qualifications At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts Copies of the required license and certifications. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered.  Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application.  Incomplete applications will not be considered. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Fall-Adjunct-Faculty--Curriculum-and-Instruction---On-Campus-_R-096081-1": {
      "title": "Fall Adjunct Faculty (Curriculum and Instruction) (On Campus)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Fall Adjunct Faculty (Curriculum and Instruction) (On Campus) Agency Texas A&M International University Department Educational Programs Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education seeks to establish a pool of qualified applicants for future, part-time Adjunct Faculty appointments in Curriculum and Instruction on campus. Successful applicants may teach up to six (6) semester credit hours within the required discipline (Language & Literature for the Young Child, Science Principles for EC-Grade 6 and Social Studies Principles for EC-Grade 6) as dictated by student demand, hold office hours, and assist students as needed. Education and Experience: Master’s degree in Education or related fields. Three years of EC-12 teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, orally and in writing. Ability to interact effectively and professionally with the general public. Ability to plan, organize, and prioritize tasks. Ability to work under stress and with pressing timelines. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Other information: The above job duties may not be performed in every Adjunct Faculty position and might not include all related duties that may be performed. Adjunct Faculty positions are temporary appointments, assigned per semester and on an as-needed basis. These temporary appointments are for the Fall 2026 semester and/or any applicable Fall 2026 Sub-terms. Initial review of applications will begin on August 12th, 2026. Application Procedure: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Completed employment applications must include: Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest addressing qualifications At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered.  Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “see resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application.  Incomplete applications will not be considered. As an employee of the State of Texas, it is your responsibility to maintain accurate contact information to include your primary work and residence addresses in your employee file located in Workday.  State of Texas employees who are approved to work outside of the state of Texas may be subject to state and local taxes of the locale in which the work is performed. Members of the Texas A&M University System must comply with those applicable state and local tax laws. In addition, the employee benefits offered with your position will be in accordance with and will not exceed those defined by Texas state law. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
