    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Clinical-Assistant-Associate-Professor-and-Director-of-the-Medical-Lab-Sciences-Program_R-093864-1": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and Director of the Medical Lab Sciences Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and Director of the Medical Lab Sciences Program Agency Texas A&M International University Department College Of Nursing & Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for a  Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and Director of the Medical Lab Sciences Program to begin  Spring 2027 .  TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/ This is a full-time, non-tenure-track, 12-month appointment, that includes both administrative and teaching responsibilities. Primary duties will include providing leadership for the implementation, administration, assessment, and continuous improvement of the BSMLS program; support programmatic accreditation activities and maintain compliance with institutional, state, and professional standards; develop, implement, assess, and revise curriculum, student learning outcomes, and program effectiveness measures; teach undergraduate Medical Laboratory Science courses and support innovative, student-centered learning environments; recruit, advise, mentor, and support students, including students from multicultural, multilingual, and first-generation backgrounds; assist with recruitment, hiring, on-boarding, mentoring, and evaluation of program faculty in collaboration with department leadership; develop and maintain partnerships with healthcare organizations and clinical affiliates to support student learning experiences and workforce development initiatives; and coordinate student clinical education experiences and support professional preparation activities. Duties also include participating in service activities at the department, college, university, professional, and community levels; and other duties as assigned by the Chair of Health Sciences. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  The selected candidate will join the TAMIU community during a period of growth and expansion in the health sciences and will provide leadership for continued implementation and growth of the BSMLS program while advancing student success, workforce development, and healthcare needs across South Texas and the border region.  The BSMLS program is approval through the Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board (THECB) and the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) Required Qualifications The successful candidate must hold an  earned master’s degree in Medical Laboratory Science, Clinical Laboratory Science, Biological Sciences, Health Sciences, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution; current national certification as a Medical Laboratory Scientist/Medical Technologist (MLS/MT) through ASCP Board of Certification or equivalent certification; minimum of five years of professional clinical laboratory experience across multiple laboratory disciplines; minimum of three years of higher education teaching, laboratory education, clinical instruction, or academic program administration experience; demonstrated knowledge of curriculum development, assessment practices, accreditation processes, and program administration; strong organizational, leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills.  We strongly encourage candidates with earned doctorate (PhD, EdD, DCLS, DHSc, or related discipline); experience with accreditation activities, program development, curriculum planning, or academic leadership; experience developing clinical partnerships and coordinating clinical education experiences; experience working with multicultural, multilingual, and first-generation student populations.  We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university. Application Process   The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/ . For more information, contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Jose Moris at jose.moris@tamiu.edu . INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Public-Administration_R-096552-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Public Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Public Administration Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Social Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Assistant Professor of Public Administration to begin  Fall 2027 .  TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/ This is a tenure-track position. Primary duties will include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Public Administration and Political Science, conducting research, and participating in governance of our NASPAA-accredited Master of Public Administration program. Duties also include serving on departmental, college, university, and professional committees as well as mentoring students. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  The Master of Public Administration program is housed within the Department of Social Sciences, which is within the College of Arts and Sciences. For more information, please visit our website at https://www.tamiu.edu/mpa/index.shtml . Required Qualifications The successful candidate must hold a PhD in Public Administration or a related field. Candidates who are ABD will also be considered but must have earned their degree before August 16, 2027. We are looking for candidates with primary research and teaching interests in program evaluation and public policy. The successful candidate will also be able to teach courses in research methods. We strongly encourage candidates with research and teaching interests that would complement our current faculty and strengthen our undergraduate and graduate programs. We are particularly interested in candidates with strong research skills, strong teaching skills, a strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals or the potential to publish in top scholarly journals, and the potential for or prior experience with seeking and/or securing external grant funding.  We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university. Application Process   The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at   https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/ . For more information, contact the search committee chair, Dr. Peter Haruna at pharuna@tamiu.edu . INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Professional-Counselor-II_R-096569-1": {
      "title": "Professional Counselor II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Professional Counselor II Agency Texas A&M International University Department Kate Marmion Counseling Center Proposed Minimum Salary $4,446.00 monthly Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Job Summary The Professional Counselor II, under general supervision, provides multiculturally competent mental health counseling and outreach to individuals, couples, and groups. May provide adjunct supervision for graduate students in counseling, counseling psychology, and graduate assistants. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provides mental health counseling as well as crisis intervention to individuals, couples, and groups. Meets ethical obligations for timely documentation of counseling services per State of Texas licensure requirements and Counseling & Psychological Services policies. Engages in counseling related activities including administering and interpreting psychological tests/inventories, making referrals, and managing various organizational and administrative aspects of counseling cases. Provides consultation to faculty, staff, students, and parents. Seeks consultation from peers and leadership for difficult clinical cases per State of Texas licensure requirements. Per state licensure requirements, participates in continuing education and professional development activities related to the performance of job functions and maintenance of skills in one’s professional specialty area. Serves on departmental committees and meetings, division and university committees, and other university functions. Provides outreach presentations for students, faculty, and staff members about counseling services, programs, professional development topics, issues, etc. Provides professional presentations at local, regional, and national conferences and workshops. May provide adjunct supervision for masters and doctoral degree graduate students in counseling, counseling psychology, and graduate assistants. May provide weekly supervision/training including review of recorded sessions and case review for provisionally licensed interns and/or practica students. Assists with organizational and administrative tasks, as requested. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. Additional Responsibilities Serve as liaison with other offices. Serve on committees. Schedule, prepare, provide, and report on conjoint and independent mental health and wellness related outreach on campus, as needed and as approved (i.e. student messaging; design/delivery strategies on posters and bulletins; workshops; information tables; class presentations; speaking assignments; etc.) Minimum Requirements Education – Master’s degree in Counseling and Guidance, Social Work, Counseling, Clinical Psychology, or other specialty related to job function. Experience – One year post Master's experience in college counseling center or other relevant setting. Preferred Education and Experience Licensure for independent practice in the State of Texas. (LPC, LCDC). Counseling and outreach experience in a university setting. Experience doing veterans counseling and/or drug/alcohol counseling. Knowledge and Abilities Knowledge of: Word processing, spreadsheet and database applications. Ability to: Multitask and work cooperatively with others. Communicate and effectively, orally and in writing. Preferred Knowledge and Abilities Knowledge of: Must possess time-management, planning, and organization skills. Ability to: Interact effectively and professionally with the University community, general public, and the students served. Work independently and follow-through on all tasks. Maintain confidentiality. Familiarity with campus-related issues (i.e., adults, women, men, Hispanic populations, adjustment, etc.) License/Professional Certification Texas Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC), Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT), or Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW). Physical Requirements – General office environment The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Supervision of Others This position generally does not supervise employees. Other Requirements Evening and/or weekend hours and rotating on-call responsibilities required. Travel may be required. Position requires on-campus, face-to-face interactions. Position requires maintaining a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace. Salary: $53,352.00/annual INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials .  The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time.  The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Be sure to include: Resume Cover Letter 3 -5 professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Chief-Human-Resources-Officer--CHRO-_R-096579-1": {
      "title": "Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO) Agency Texas A&M International University Department Human Resources Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO) serves as the University's senior human resources executive and strategic advisor to the Vice President for Finance & Administration/Chief Financial Officer on all matters related to human capital management. The CHRO provides visionary leadership for a comprehensive human resources program that attracts, develops, engages, and retains a highly qualified workforce while advancing the University's strategic priorities and ensuring compliance with applicable federal and state laws, Texas A&M University System Regulations, and University Rules.   This executive leads a customer-focused Human Resources organization committed to operational excellence, continuous improvement, innovation, and exceptional service while helping position Texas A&M International University as an employer of choice. Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Include: Executive Leadership Serves as a member of the Vice President for Finance & Administration leadership team. Advises executive leadership on workforce strategy and organizational effectiveness. Leads enterprise-wide workforce planning initiatives. Serves advisor to executive leadership on organizational change. Presents HR initiatives and recommendations to executive leadership and, when appropriate, the President and Board of Regents. Builds strategic partnerships across the University and the Texas A&M University System. Organizational Effectiveness Organizational design Business process improvement Workforce analytics Change management Executive coaching Culture assessment Employee engagement strategy Leadership effectiveness Succession planning Workforce productivity Compensation Executive compensation recommendations Market salary studies Internal equity reviews Classification strategy Recruitment incentives Retention strategies Workforce analytics Compensation philosophy Recruitment Employer branding Recruiting Recruitment marketing Candidate experience Workforce forecasting Talent pipeline development Time-to-fill metrics Quality-of-hire metrics HR Technology Leadership HRIS modernization Workflow automation Digital HR processes HR dashboards Executive metrics AI-assisted HR technologies where appropriate Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Ten years progressively responsible HR leadership Five years leading professional HR staff Experience in organizational development Experience leading compensation programs Experience managing organizational change Experience advising executive leadership Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree Higher education experience Texas public higher education experience Texas A&M System experience • HRCI, SHRM-SCP, or SPHR certification preferred Experience leading HR transformation Experience implementing HR technology Experience with compensation studies • Experience supporting executive leadership Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strategic Leadership Executive Presence Emotional Intelligence Business Acumen Financial Acumen Data Analytics Negotiation Conflict Resolution Change Leadership Organizational Development Influence Without Authority Executive Communication Key Leadership Traits and Characteristics Defined Strategic - Thinks beyond HR administration and connects people, talent, and organizational decisions to the university's mission, growth, and strategic priorities. Collaborative - Builds partnerships across academic and administrative units and works with leaders to accomplish objectives rather than functioning as a roadblock. Approachable & Relationship-Oriented - Visible, accessible, personable, and able to create an environment where faculty, staff, and leaders are comfortable engaging HR. Transparent & Communicative - Communicates openly, clearly, consistently, and respectfully; explains decisions and creates confidence in HR processes. Emotionally Intelligent & Empathetic – Listens genuinely, demonstrates tact and self-awareness, understands how actions and communication affect others, and handles difficult situations with maturity. Integrity, Fairness & Consistency – Leads with integrity and sound judgment, approaching decisions with fairness, transparency, and consistency while fostering confidence and positive relationships across the University. Solutions-Oriented & Adaptable - Looks for ways to accomplish institutional objectives, challenges unnecessary barriers, welcomes new ideas, and adjusts effectively as circumstances change. Empowering People Leader – Develops the HR team, delegates appropriately, builds capabilities, encourages professional growth, creates accountability, and develops future leaders Success Expectations Initial and Longer-Term Strategic Priorities: The following priorities reflect areas in which the new CHRO will be expected to provide leadership over time. They are not intended to suggest that each initiative must be completed during the first year. Early success will include listening to and engaging the University community, assessing current practices and needs, establishing priorities, and developing a thoughtful sequence for implementation. Some initiatives may begin immediately, while others will appropriately develop over the CHRO’s first several years. Develop a University Workforce Strategic Plan. Lead a comprehensive review of compensation and classification. Continue efforts to strengthen employee engagement. Review and modernize HR policies and procedures as appropriate. Identify opportunities to improve recruitment processes and reduce cycle times. Strengthen leadership development opportunities. Develop a thoughtful approach to succession planning. Advance HR technology and process automation. Continue to strengthen HR service and customer satisfaction. NOMINATIONS & APPLICATIONS The Search Committee invites letters of interest and nominations to be submitted directly to the search firm Anthem Executive | Anthem Academics. Correspondence should include a curriculum vitae and a letter of interest describing relevant experience and interest in the position. Submit materials to Michael Ballew, Scott Watson, JR Wheless, or Florene Stawowy at: CHROTAMIU@AnthemExecutive.com While applications and nominations will be accepted until a CHRO is selected, interested parties are strongly encouraged to submit their materials as soon as possible to assure consideration. Anthem and the University reserve the right to end or extend the application and nomination process at any time. Expressing interest is the first step in receiving consideration and does not make one an applicant for the position. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-Station-TX/Instructional-Design-Librarian--Assistant-or-Associate-_R-095655-3": {
      "title": "Instructional Design Librarian (Assistant or Associate)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructional Design Librarian (Assistant or Associate) Agency Texas A&M University Department Libraries Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location College Station, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description A Glimpse of the Job Join us in shaping the future of online learning at Texas A&M Libraries! Texas A&M Libraries is seeking an Assistant Librarian or an Associate Librarian to join our innovative team focused on advancing information literacy and student success through engaging online learning experiences. In this role, you'll collaborate with librarians, faculty, and subject matter experts to design and deliver impactful online tutorials and learning resources using tools such as Canvas, Articulate 360, and multimedia technologies. You'll play a key role in developing accessible, evidence-based learning experiences that connect students with library resources, services, and essential research skills. You'll be empowered with exceptional resources, including the collaboration of a dedicated Instructional Designer and access to a state-of-the-art multimedia studio for creating high-quality learning content. Experience in academic, school, or special libraries is valued, as is a passion for learner-centered design, accessibility, collaboration, and student success. Join a team committed to transforming how students learn, discover, and succeed. Interested in this role? Join us for an informational session for the First Year Information Literacy Librarian and Instructional Design Librarian positions on August 24th at 1pm central time via the following link: https://tamu.libcal.com/event/17372702 What You Need to Know Salary – Assistant Librarian: $62,900/annually Salary – Associate Librarian: $72,335/annually Please note this is an in-person, on-site role located in College Station, TX. Portfolio: An online portfolio demonstrating examples of online learning development is strongly recommended. (Coursework examples are acceptable too.) You can include your portfolio in the CV/Resume section. Cover Letter/Resume: A cover letter and resume are strongly recommended and will help in our review. Qualifications Assistant Librarian - Required Education and Experience: Master’s degree in Library Science. No prior experience required. Associate Librarian - Required Education and Experience: Master’s degree in Library Science. 5 years related experience. A Well-Qualified Candidate Will Also Possess: Experience or coursework related to implementing a cohesive tutorial program in either a K-12 setting or an academic library setting. Experience with collaborating effectively with stakeholders such as faculty, staff, students, and/or administrators. Experience or coursework related to implementing accessibility standards, including web accessibility standards (WCAG) and ADA requirements in educational contexts. Experience or coursework using modern e-Learning authoring and multimedia production tools such as Articulate Storyline, Rise, Adobe Captivate, H5P, Camtasia, Adobe Creative Cloud, Vyond, or equivalent tools. Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Ability to communicate with all levels of customers and employees. Ability to prioritize multiple projects and manage time effectively. Opportunities to Contribute Online Learning Development - Participates in the development of the University Libraries’ tutorial program and online learning initiatives using tools such as Texas A&M’s course management systems (Canvas), Articulate 360, and other multimedia tools. Designs, produces, and maintains multimedia instructional content, including video tutorials, interactive modules, infographics, and other digital learning objects. Maintains knowledge of emerging trends in online learning and provides recommendations of new technologies or services to library leadership. Ensures digital learning meets accessibility standards and evidence based-pedagogical best practices. Collaborates with regional and local locations at the University Libraries on access of Library collections and improving virtual learning for distance learners. Collaborations & Partnerships - Participates in unit meetings and interdepartmental activities throughout the Libraries. Collaborates with colleagues on design, delivery, assessment, and promotion of library programs that support information literacy and student success. Participates in the improvement of the Libraries’ online learning instruction focusing on information literacy, learning theory, and student development in online environments. Actively engages and supports Library and TAMU initiatives. Contribution to the Profession - Participates in scholarly activities and professional service for professional development and to incorporate new ideas and technologies into library services and programs. Serves on campus and library committees and engages with campus units to advocate for Library presence in online learning. Who We Are The Libraries are the indispensable hub of discovery, learning and creativity with the teaching and research that goes on in the colleges and academic departments. We offer rich and extraordinary collections at the University Libraries. The Libraries resources and services enable and support the University missions of teaching, research, and service. Learn more about our various libraries at  https://library.tamu.edu Why Texas A&M University? We are a prestigious university with strong traditions, Core Values, and a community of caring and collaboration. Amenities associated with a major university, such as sporting and cultural events, state-of-the-art recreation facilities, the Bush Library and Museum, and much more await you. Experience all that a big city has to offer but with a reasonable cost-of-living and no long commutes.   Medical,   prescription drug,   dental,   vision,   life and AD&D,   flexible spending accounts ,  and long-term disability insurance  with Texas A&M contributing to employee health and basic life premiums  12-15 days  of annual paid holidays   Up to  eight hours of paid sick leave  and at least  eight hours of paid vacation  each month  Automatic enrollment in the  Teacher Retirement System of Texas    Health and Wellness:  Free exercise programs and release time   Professional Development: All employees have access to free  LinkedIn Learning  training, webinars, and limited financial support to attend conferences, workshops, and more   Educational release time and tuition assistance  for completing a degree while a Texas A&M employee  Living Well,  a program at Texas A&M that has been built by employees, for employees  Our Commitment Texas A&M University is committed to enriching the learning and working environment by promoting a culture that respects all perspectives, talents & lived experiences. Embracing varying opinions and perspectives strengthens our  core   values  which are: Respect, Excellence, Leadership, Loyalty, Integrity, and Selfless Service.    All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Program-Specialist-I_R-096454-1": {
      "title": "Program Specialist I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Program Specialist I Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Fine & Performing Arts Proposed Minimum Salary $17.54 hourly Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Job Summary   The Program Specialist I, under general supervision, performs entry-level specialist duties for a department, college, or division.           Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assists in planning, developing, implementing, coordinating, and monitoring programs and services. Plans and develops specialized programs such as conferences, seminars, lectures, meetings, and workshops to facilitate program goals. Coordinates specialized program communications and marketing materials. Assists in the development of policies and procedures. Assists in the preparation and maintenance of budgets, special reports, and other documents.  Attends meetings and conferences to discuss the progress of assigned programs. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned.           Additional Duties and Responsibilities Coordinates departmental events and activities, including concerts, recitals, auditions, exhibitions, lectures, and special programs. Assists with scheduling facilities and managing ongoing schedule changes related to departmental programming. Coordinates guest artist logistics and works with university offices to facilitate contracts, agreements, and related documentation. Works with university offices and external organizations to support scheduling, contracts, approvals, purchasing, event logistics, and other administrative processes with minimal supervision. Supports departmental communications and promotional efforts in collaboration with University Public Relations, including event announcements, programs, posters, website updates and social media content. Serves as a point of contact for faculty, students, staff, and external partners regarding departmental events and activities. Maintains records, manages and monitors multiple projects, deadlines, and approvals to ensure timely completion of assigned tasks. Attends meetings and conferences to departmental initiatives.           Minimum Requirements Education – Bachelor’s degree in related field such as Arts Administration, Communications, Marketing, Business, or a closely related discipline. Experience – No prior experience required.        Preferred Education and Experience       Experience - One year of administrative, event coordination, customer service, office support, or related experience. Supporting academic programs, events, or arts-related operations in a higher education or arts organization setting.           Knowledge and Abilities           Knowledge of: Word processing and spreadsheet applications. Ability to: Multitask and work cooperatively with others. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and customer service skills. Maintains attention to detail and utilizes sound judgment.         Preferred Knowledge and Abilities          Knowledge of event coordination, scheduling processes, contract administration, and marketing and promotional workflows. Ability to coordinate multiple activities, deadlines, and administrative processes simultaneously. Communicate effectively with faculty, students, staff, and external partners. Adapt to frequent schedule changes while maintaining attention to detail and follow-through. Ability to support event promotion through social media and other communication channels.           Licensing / Professional Certification – None           Physical Requirements – General office environment The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Supervision of Others           This position generally does not supervise employees.   Other Requirements           Evening and weekend work may occasionally be required. Position requires on campus, face-to-face interactions. Position requires maintaining a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace. Salary: $17.54/hour INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials .  The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time.  The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Be sure to include: Resume Cover Letter 3 -5 professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Coach--Softball-_R-096052": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach (Softball)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Coach (Softball) Agency Texas A&M International University Department Athletics Department Proposed Minimum Salary $3,040.27 monthly Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Job Summary The Assistant Coach (Softball) provides assistance to the head coach with all areas of team administration and management, including practice sessions, conditioning workouts, monitoring of student-athletes academic progress, and evaluation and recruiting of prospective student-athletes for the team. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist the head coach and other staff members with routine administrative responsibilities of the assigned sport program and management of the men/women’s team. Coaches, at the direction of the head coach, provide instruction, demonstration and teaching the sport's dynamics to student-athletes to ensure maximum potential of individuals and the team as a whole. Recruit and scout prospective student-athletes from high school, junior and community colleges Make recommendations to the head coach regarding potential of student-athletes. Stay current, understand, and adhere to all NCAA guidelines and maintain up-to-date rosters, squad lists, and other information using the Compliance Assistant Internet (CAI) program and ARMS software. Assist in coordinating and developing organized schedules and submitting weekly countable hours report according to NCAA policy.  Will report any violations of these established rules, which may arise, to the proper officials. Assist head coach in coordinating team travel, arranging competitive schedule, organizing and scheduling practice sessions, updating and maintaining student-athlete recruiting databases, updating and maintaining files (both hard copy and video) of opponents. Assist in implementing and maintaining a comprehensive public relations program. Assist in managing the operations of sport camps and/or clinics. Assist in managing all department fund-raising and booster events in accordance with NCAA, Lone Star Conference, and institutional rules, policies, and procedures Establish and ensure communication and enforcement of rules and regulations concerning student-athlete conduct, appearance, road games, punctuality and other areas. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. Additional Responsibilities Assist in ensuring satisfactory academic performance of student-athletes. Manages study hall hours and coordinates with the academic advisers to monitor and support student-athletes’ academic progress. Minimum Requirements Education – Bachelor's degree for a regionally accredited institution of higher education. Experience – One year of previous high school, collegiate or higher-level coaching. Knowledge and Abilities Knowledge of: General knowledge of NCAA rules.   Word processing, spreadsheet, and database programs. Ability to: Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Oral and written communication skills. Licensing / Professional Certification - None Physical Requirements – General Office and Athletic Facilities Environment. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Supervision of Others This position may supervise employees and student athletes. Other Requirements Position requires travel. Evening and weekend work required. Position requires on campus, face-to-face interactions. Position requires maintaining a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace. Applicants are subject to an NCAA enforcement staff compliance review, and employment is contingent upon satisfactory results. Salary: $36,483.24/annual INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials .  The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time.  The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Be sure to include: Resume Cover Letter 3 -5 professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Task-Worker-II--Athletics-_R-096158": {
      "title": "Task Worker II (Athletics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Task Worker II (Athletics) Agency Texas A&M International University Department Athletics Department Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Temporary/Casual Staff (Fixed Term) Job Description Job Summary The Task Worker (Game Staff) will provide event support to the designated sport as directed by the Sports Information Director.   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide event support to designated sport as directed by the Sports Information Director. Duties included, but are not limited to, media liaison, gym floor maintenance, referee liaison, and game equipment management. Perform other related duties as assigned.   Minimum Requirement Education - High school graduate or equivalent. Experience - No previous experience required May not be currently enrolled as an undergraduate student at Texas A&M International University.   Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:   Knowledge of: Strong customer service skills   Ability to: Interact effectively and professionally with the general public. Work under stress and with pressing timelines. Communicate effectively, orally and in writing. Preferred Licensing / Professional Certification None Physical Requirements – None The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.   Other Information Position is temporary, assigned per game/event and on an as-needed basis. The above job duties may not be performed in every task worker position and may not include all related duties that might be performed. Position requires working days, evenings, and/or weekends of home games/events. Position requires strict punctuality to arrive to work promptly at the scheduled time. Position requires on campus, face-to-face interactions. Position requires maintaining a regular schedule of attendance in the workplace. Pay of Rate : $15.00 per hour for up to 15 hours weekly, based on assigned event/game as needed. INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials .  The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time.  The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Be sure to include: Resume/CV Cover Letter 3-5 professional references and their full contact information and Unofficial transcripts Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Chief-of-Police_R-095951-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Chief of Police",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Chief of Police Agency Texas A&M International University Department University Police Department Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Job Summary The Assistant Chief of Police, under direction, oversees general administration for all law enforcement functions assigned to Field Operations within the Department of Security and University Police. Ensures that programs are in place to maximize security of people and property on campus. In the absence of the Chief, may assume overall responsibility for the operation of the department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Monitors and evaluates the efficiency and effectiveness of police service methods and procedures and recommends appropriate service and staffing levels. Responds to and resolves difficult and sensitive citizen inquires and complaints. Responds to questions and information requests from the public. Manages services and activities of assigned functional area. Coordinates the activities of personnel in preserving order, protecting life and property, investigating crimes, and enforcing state laws. Supervises assigned staff. Serves as backup to the Chief of Police. Assists in the development of departmental goals, objectives, policies and procedures. Formulates rules, procedures and standards for assigned divisions and ensures they are maintained. Ensures compliance with all local, state, and federal reporting requirements. Responds to requests for information from government agencies and the general public. Conducts and completes special projects. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. Additional Responsibilities Maintaining department’s accreditation which may include but is not limited to review and updating of department’s policies and standing general orders. Minimum Requirements Education – Bachelor’s degree. Experience – Ten years as a Certified Peace Officer. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Preferred Education and Experience 15 years as a Certified Peace Officer with experience in higher education campus law enforcement. Knowledge and Abilities Knowledge of: Word processing and spreadsheet applications. Thorough knowledge of Criminal Justice System. Leadership and management abilities.   Ability to: Multitask and work cooperatively with others. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills. Communicate effectively with all segments of the campus population. Function under adverse and stressful conditions. Preferred Knowledge and Abilities Internal Affairs Licensing / Professional Certification Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) Master Peace Officer Certification Must have a State of Texas class \"C\" vehicle operator's license or ability to obtain within 30 days of employment. Firearms Proficiency Physical Requirements – None. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Supervision of Others This position generally supervises employees. Other Requirements All System University police will be required to meet minimum licensing standard requirements as required by the Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) § 217.1. Work beyond normal office hours and/or work on weekends. Position requires on-campus, face-to-face interactions. Position requires maintaining a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  Must successfully pass psychological evaluation, physical examination, and complete background investigation to include but not limited to driving history, criminal background, and credit history. Salary: $80,000-$92,000/annual INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials .  The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time.  The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Be sure to include: Resume Cover Letter 3 -5 professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts (if applicable) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
